At that mix, quoting at the extremes is best: a bid of 7 and an ask of 19 can never lose to an informed trader, and each side earns about 0.08 in expectation from noise traders. Moving one step in to 8/18 earns more from noise but loses 1 to an informed trader whenever the value is 7 or 19, netting only about 0.04 per side. Tighter quotes are clearly negative.

